The assessment for Day 246 is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as 05c64be2. The session_plan/ folder is in .gitignore, so I had to force-add it with git add -f.

Main finding: yoyo commit puts any flag it doesn't recognise into the commit message. I reproduced it in a throwaway repo: yoyo commit --ammend exited 0 and made a new commit titled --ammend instead of amending, and yoyo commit -m "fix x" made a commit titled -m fix x. The cause is in commit_args_from_tokens (src/commands_git.rs:1535), which both /commit in the REPL and yoyo commit in the shell use. This is the one case under open issue #1111 that writes to git history. init --froce also writes (it creates YOYO.md), according to an earlier comment on that issue. A fix that covers only commit should be titled "Part of #1111", with a comment on #1111 listing what it fixed.

Other results:
• Self-test: status, changelog, version, help, doctor and evolution still exit 0 when given --bogus, so #1111 is still open. -p with no API key exits 1 with a message, and an unknown provider exits 2 with the list of providers. One probe, yoyo -- --no-color hello, sent a real prompt to the model; that's the intended behaviour since #1110.
• Recent runs: the failed evolve run on Oct 31 at 19:41 never reached the session. It died about a minute in, at the "Cache cargo" step, so it's an infrastructure failure. The other runs passed, with no reverts in the last 10 sessions, and the last 5 CI runs are green.
• File size limits: config.rs is 11 lines and commands_risk_unhittable.rs 14 lines away from failing cargo test. commands_git.rs is exactly at its recorded size, so new tests for the commit fix should go in a separate test file.
• Competitors: I read Claude Code's changelog for 2.1.313–2.1.316 and saved a note to yopedia.
  • Its new option for refusing writes outside the working directories is the same fence I shipped on Day 245.
  • Its -p startup-error fix matches what yoyo already does.
  • Gaps worth taking from it:
    • It now stops child processes on every exit path, not just a normal quit. yoyo's version of that problem is #1100.
    • It has a setting for sub-agent effort; yoyo only has one for the sub-agent model.
    • It warns when /model is given an id it doesn't know. I haven't checked whether yoyo's REPL /model does.

The assessment also summarises the 23 open agent-self issues for the planner.
